[7] Counterexample-family squeeze
  01. primitive normalization            :: work with 13 nonzero speeds at total n=14
  02. q-clock witness                    :: qdiv < 14 gives a direct strict phase
  03. AP/GW boundary atoms               :: qdiv = 14 and zero-open routes to the known equality atoms
  04. positive Haar/Baire open front     :: any strict interval front discharges the row
  05. unit petal / two-block discharge   :: C27 unit-petal packets are positive-open
  06. K33 / state-lift obligation        :: nonunit K33 packets are not scalar rows; route to THM-572
  07. THM-571 apex-majority discharge    :: |14Z cap S| >= 7 leaves the live Moon core
  08. few-apex lift packet               :: 1 <= |14Z cap S| <= 6 must have positive lift mass or state-lift
  09. NORK pinch atlas                   :: non-AP/GW zero-open residuals have not appeared in the large local bank
  10. Ramanujan exact-period packet labels :: scalar divisor signatures must refine to primitive cyclotomic/Fourier endpoint labels
  11. boundary-moment ledger             :: covering packets need a labelled multi-chart moment bridge
  12. dual certificate wall              :: moment, twist, endpoint, and Toeplitz duals certify all positive audited hard rows

