[9] Synthesis theorem target
  Finite proof-object sheaf theorem for LRC14:
    Every primitive 13-speed row reaches one of the named sheaf exits:
    q-witness, AP/GW boundary equality, unit-petal discharge,
    K33/state-lift obligation, positive boundary/lift packet,
    fixed-margin labelled family discharge, Ramanujan/cyclotomic
    exact-period quotient-admissibility packet, or a dual certificate from endpoint
    potential, multiplicity moment, danger-count moment, rational twist,
    or Fourier-Toeplitz negativity.
  A proposed counterexample must be invisible to every current quotient;
  the remaining work is to prove that invisibility forces AP/GW or a
  named state-lift packet, not a new scalar extremizer.
